WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:05.100
So, how did you get tricked into coming here?

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.480
I heard there's a secret furniture shop here.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.590
Even a kid would've seen through that lie.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:18.370
Today's a surprise get-together
 to get you two back on good terms again.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.660
Gayus and I have a gentleman's agreement

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.000
that ensures we don't become 
friendly with each other.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.500
He's right.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.250
We're cooperating in order 
to not get along, which means...

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.250
So you're on good terms after all?

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.210
Or bad?

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.080
Huh?

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.640
Hey, it's Jivenya.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.400
Jabeira.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.630
Been a while.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.890
It's been ages.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.770
It's the four-eyed loser
 and the Draken dumbass.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.530
Huh? What?

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:29.000
<b>Endgame of Sand</b>

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:32.290
Jabeira helped me out a lot 
when I first joined the company.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:36.840
You're still adorable, 
even though you left us.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.200
I didn't think <i>you</i> would be
 her boyfriend though, Gayus.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.180
What? Got a problem with that?

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:46.480
Say, Jabeira, who's this?

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.220
Is he your boyfriend?

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.440
No!

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.310
I'm just a fellow Jushikiist.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:56.300
Oh, you're so cold, Iegie.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.950
D-D-Don't touch me when
you're in old fart mode!

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.230
Damn...

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:04.070
By the way, how's Largonkin doing?

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:07.200
He'll be ready to leave
the hospital soon, thanks to you.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.630
My old man isn't croaking that easily.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.960
Oh? Did someone get hurt?

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.490
Czahn!

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.480
Long time no see.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.470
Over here.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.840
Czahn...

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:22.840
What's your relationship with her?

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.580
Jabeira and I are cousins.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:29.180
A multiple personality weirdo

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.730
and a deviant doctor with an organ fetish.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:34.610
Your family sure is cursed.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:36.680
My, how rude.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:39.690
Hey, I have a great idea!

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:43.360
Since you're here, why not join us?

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.070
One, two, three...

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.110
Four, five, six...

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:51.750
Is this really supposed to be fun?

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.120
You know how it goes with these games.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.600
So... Seven, eight, nine.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.730
Ten, eleven, twelve.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:59.440
<i>Jiv probably doesn't know,</i>

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.640
Thirteen, fourteen, fifteen.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:03.690
<i>but nothing good happens when when 
Offensive Jushikiists get together to drink.</i>

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.840
Sixteen, seventeen, eighteen.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.890
Nineteen, twenty, twenty-one.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:07.950
<i>That is to say, eight times out of ten,
 there's bloodshed.</i>

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.950
Twenty-two, twenty-three, twenty-four.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:10.140
Twenty-five, twenty-six, twenty-seven.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:13.020
<i>So, being as clever as I am,
 I came up with a game.</i>

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.000
<i>The rules are simple.</i>

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:17.990
<i>Each person counts numbers in order.</i>

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:23.150
<i>The person who calls out one hundred 
loses and gets a punishment.</i>

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.170
<i>You can call up to three numbers at a time.</i>

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:30.940
<i>And the most interesting part of this game...</i>

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:34.020
Um...

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.170
Ninety-seven.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.040
Sorry, my patient.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.920
Ninety-eight, ninety-nine.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.930
Right off the bat?

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:46.800
One hundred.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.180
<i>Losing is part of my plan.</i>

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:54.690
<i>The loser's punishment is chosen 
at the winners' discretion.</i>

00:04:55.050 --> 00:05:00.150
<i>Naturally, the game becomes more and more 
vicious and merciless as it goes on.</i>

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:07.450
<i>Which means that the person who loses 
at the beginning suffers the least.</i>

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:17.320
And so, Patient 49707015

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:20.960
will suffer a public display of his organs.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.800
Shoot...

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:28.490
I forgot how unpopular I was.

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:29.370
Agh...

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:31.200
Not to worry.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.470
This is my precious treasure.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:36.230
It cuts amazingly well.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.580
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:42.110
Oh dear, she's back already.

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:47.610
Gigina, you lied about 
my neighbor's place being on fire!

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.340
Huh, I must have misheard.

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:54.120
This is mine!

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.120
Don't touch it!

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:00.330
By "it," which part do you mean?

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:01.460
His pancreas?

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:04.300
I can vouch for that.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:08.760
Nah, Czahn, she cares about 
something a bit lower.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.260
That's not the only thing!

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.410
It's all important to me, including that!

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:18.810
So everything <i>including</i> his penis.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.720
Okay, okay!

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:25.020
No lethal weapons.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:25.820
Okay?

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.510
Shall we move on to the next match, then?

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:30.240
Bring it on!

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.000
Hey... guys...

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:37.220
<i>Now it's time for round two...</i>

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.090
<i>Time for my revenge.</i>

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:40.090
Ninety-three, ninety-four...

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:43.290
Are you okay?

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.670
Okay, I'll go with ninety-five.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:52.480
In that case, ninety-six.

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:53.720
You bastard!

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.100
You did this on purpose!

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:58.140
Ninety-seven, ninety-eight, ninety-nine!

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.970
There! You lose, Gigina.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:06.440
M-M-M... My... My...

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.380
Louder.

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:14.580
M-My bride-to-be is an a-amazing woman.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.450
I-I-I...

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:18.700
"I"?

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:21.820
I love...

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.720
<i>Czahn lost the third round.</i>

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.670
Ninety-four.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:35.850
Ninety-five.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:37.400
Ninety-six.

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:39.780
Ninety-seven.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:42.230
Ninety-eight.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:44.080
Don't worry about me.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.480
I'll be fine.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:47.980
Ninety-nine.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.160
Jabeira!

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.730
Blame Gayus if you're upset.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.570
Now say one hundred.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:59.390
Oink! Oink!

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:01.550
Oink! Oink!

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:03.690
You don't sound serious enough.

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:07.560
Piglets wouldn't have such a scary face.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:09.110
Be cuter.

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:11.590
Come on, she's had enough.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:13.090
Enough?

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:15.470
Now!

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:16.970
Oink!

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:18.220
Squeal some more!

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:22.200
Cry in the subservience and sorrow 
that is the life of an artiodactyl!

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.470
M-My precious...

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:27.700
Say, Gayus...

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:29.730
Don't say it.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.240
<i>As it turns out, 
Offensive Jushikiists can cooperate,</i>

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.150
<i>but we can't get along.</i>

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.620
<i>The hellish game continued.</i>

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:41.210
Round ten!

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:43.620
This'll be the last one.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.770
Who's going first?

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.520
Are you okay with this?

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:50.990
Your girlfriend's been more than 
a little bit messed up ever since...

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:52.600
Piss off, Iegie.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:57.760
Piss me off, and your penalty 
will be public masturbation.

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:03.520
If you're scared, you may as well 
shove your head up your ass and cower.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:06.970
Sadly, the time for games is over.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.440
This place is already a 
gambling parlor of hell.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.770
A battlefield.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:19.900
Bippity boppity albertacadabra!

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:23.040
Old hag magical girl Jabby Jabeira

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:29.470
will grant all of your moronic dreams 
and filthy wishes with devious Jushiki!

00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:31.450
Not for free, of course.

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:34.550
I'm scared!

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:36.550
Don't look.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:40.710
Why was I even born?

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.430
Is this the peak Offensive Jushikiist
 life I've worked so hard for?

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.810
No, absolutely not!

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.190
But... but...

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:52.110
This is cursed.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:54.070
This is literally hell on earth.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.070
Jabeira.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:58.320
Jiv...

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:00.570
That's enough...

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:02.580
of practicing.

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:09.130
The masses need the old hag magical girl!

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:12.090
They're probably going to 
need a doctor after this.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:16.720
Not even my future bride 
is that much of a monster.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:20.570
Still, I'm glad Jiv took everyone with her.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:22.720
Have you noticed?

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:23.690
Yeah.

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:26.220
The incident is over.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.520
What use would they have for us now?

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:43.330
Now, this invitation comes 
on rather short notice.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:46.080
Are we having a surprise party of some sort?

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:49.080
Are you the heroes who saved Eridana?

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:52.460
I thought it was about time 
for our heroes' welcome,

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:54.460
Queen Xenobia.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:58.720
I thought I'd throw you a belated celebration.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.640
I'm honored.

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:03.450
It was all thanks to the 
information that you gave us.

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:05.100
Information, you say?

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:06.790
Yes.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:11.600
You were the one who had Parumuwei 
the arms dealer report the location

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:13.760
of the Aurora Hammer's hideout, were you not?

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:16.110
And since Parumuwei was 
no longer of use to you,

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.740
you got rid of him, making it look as though

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:20.600
it was the Aurora Hammer's doing.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:24.760
Well, well, what a clever young man.

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:25.740
I see.

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:29.000
It's no wonder that Mouldeen 
was interested in you.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:33.000
There's one thing that I've 
been trying to figure out

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.690
since I confronted Zhuo Lu at that hideout.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:36.500
What's that?

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:40.840
Zhuo Lu said that the Aurora Hammer's
 original form, the Aurora Front,

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:43.880
was established by the Dragon Empire.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:46.500
In that case, why would 
you want to get rid of it?

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:51.000
You created the organization in secret 
to interfere with Urmun's internal affairs.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.950
Nothing would have been more convenient

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:56.100
than to have Remedius,
a civilian, take it over.

00:11:57.220 --> 00:11:58.900
Is that your only question?

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:01.420
No, more than that,

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:04.410
why was Remedius so spiteful towards 
Rahzel and the Dragon Empire?

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:08.470
Saying it's a terrible
betrayal and backstabbing...

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.450
No...

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:13.920
It can't be.

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:15.920
So that's what it is.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:20.820
The Dragon Empire has plans to conspire 
with Dochetta... with that demon?

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:24.960
I trust that you're aware 
that the primary industry

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:27.530
of this nation is in various 
Jushiki industries.

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:29.850
It's not an overstatement to say

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:33.440
that our economy is held up by 
cutting-edge Jushiki technologies.

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:37.940
But to create those products, 
we need resources.

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:40.640
I'll get to the point.

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:42.670
The Dragon Empire and 
the Seven-City Alliance

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:45.450
embrace Dochetta's autocratic regime.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.700
In return, we share mining rights

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.830
to their underground resources: 
their rare metals.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:55.130
Then why not join forces 
with the Aurora Hammer?

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:56.010
For a more democratic...

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:57.330
That's why.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:59.200
The Aurora Hammer has declared

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:02.940
that Urmun's resources belong 
to the people of Urmun.

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:05.340
We have no need for such a government.

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:07.840
The Dragon Empire won't compromise.

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:13.350
Therefore, it was imperative 
that Remedius die as a hostage.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.230
As a hostage?

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:16.960
What do you mean by that?

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:21.860
In order to protect our nation's economy 
and the everyday lives of our people,

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:25.550
as royalty of the Dragon Empire, 
I will do anything.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.640
No matter how vile.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:32.010
It doesn't matter to me that the people 
of another nation may suffer for it.

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:35.870
I have absolutely no 
sympathy for those fools

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:38.650
who can't solve their own 
nation's problems by themselves.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:40.110
And you call yourself...

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:43.680
This decision was made by Mouldeen.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:46.380
At the secret meeting with 
the Seven-City Alliance

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:49.290
that you escorted him to.

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:56.140
You're... You're Mouldeen.

00:13:56.140 --> 00:14:00.090
The whole of the Dragon Empire's 
imperial family is a man-eating dragon.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:03.450
I'll ask one last question.

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:07.030
Why are you revealing the truth to us now?

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.400
For amusement's sake.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:12.140
I wanted to see the faces of the men

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:16.350
who survived that freak's conspiracy.

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:18.670
But it wasn't as amusing as I thought.

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:22.190
Damn...

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:24.300
They left me with some harsh words.

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:28.870
The young are so tactless.

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:31.200
Your Highness, it's time.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:32.470
All right.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:50.320
How were Gayus and Gigina?

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:55.200
To be honest, I don't understand 
why you think so highly of them.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.950
You sure are harsh with your words, my cousin.

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:03.710
You brought your Winged Generals 
to this silly public display?

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:05.050
I did.

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:08.760
It's about to begin.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:12.880
This ceremony is going to be broadcast 
to the Dragon Empire, too, apparently.

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:14.970
Now, smile, smile.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:24.720
<i>Tomorrow will bring pleasant, 
clear skies to Eridana.</i>

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:26.860
<i>It'll be a good day for doing the laundry.</i>

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:29.840
This is one unsatisfying ending.

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:31.930
We've done what we can.

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:33.260
That's all there is to it.

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:34.620
Yeah.

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:38.870
Zhuo Lu.

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:41.120
So he <i>is</i> alive.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:43.770
<i>We're live from the Urmun Republic.</i>

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:45.900
<i>There's a massive celebration 
for President Dochetta</i>

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:48.630
<i>at the palace parade grounds.</i>

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:58.430
Dochetta! Dochetta! Dochetta!

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.990
Are you unharmed, my cousin?

00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:23.880
I've survived such assassination 
attempts countless times with Jushiki.

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:29.800
I am—Urmun is—eternal!

00:16:47.260 --> 00:16:50.190
<i>Wh-What's going on?</i>

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:51.940
<i>What is that Jushiki?</i>

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:57.950
Dochetta will suffer a miserable 
death befitting of his actions.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.120
The Ava Dorn Jushiki.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.850
What do you think you're doing?

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:05.460
Wasn't your goal to take revenge 
on Rahzel and the Dragon Empire?

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:09.600
The failure of my attack 
on Rahzel was as planned.

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:12.110
The true goal of launching the warheads

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:14.480
was to create a distraction as I transferred

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:17.240
the abundance of weapons bought 
from Parumuwei to Urmun.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:21.920
To make everyone believe Remedius's 
game board was here in Eridana,

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:26.600
and to play the Great Magatsushiki, 
Dragon's Jaw, and you two.

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:30.110
But Urmun is the true game board.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:39.120
The winning condition of chells 
is not to defeat the queen,

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.870
but to defeat the king.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:45.900
Is it not clear, then, whether 
the warhead ought to be used

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:47.540
on Rahzel or Dochetta?

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:54.170
With the tyrant defeated, 
the people of Urmun will stand,

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:57.130
and a new nation will be born.

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:01.640
Whose ideology is that, Zhuo Lu?

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:04.360
Or rather, Count Remedius?

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:11.360
Remedius Levvi Rahzel is my former self.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:15.400
But now, I'm nothing but the Man-Eating 
Dragon of the Sand, Zhuo Lu.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:17.580
Man-Eating Dragon, my ass.

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:21.780
You had your own people killed in 
your place at the hostage exchange.

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:24.410
Just to save your own life.

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:28.840
Did you think I would do 
such a wasteful thing?

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:31.150
The corpse that was assumed to be Remedius

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:33.610
was a traitor with connections 
to the Dragon Empire:

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:36.420
the former leader of the Aurora Front, Zemunn.

00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:39.680
Why would you do such a thing?

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:41.150
Why?

00:18:41.150 --> 00:18:44.840
Are you suggesting that there's 
another way to defeat the oppressors

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:46.680
and take back freedom and peace?

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:50.970
How can you talk about freedom
when you've killed innocent Eridanians?

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:52.060
What do you mean, "peace"?

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:58.070
Your very existence causes the death 
of the exploited people of the desert.

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:00.730
I won't let you say you aren't responsible.

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:01.570
But...

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.760
Then propose an alternative.

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:07.080
What other way is there to 
save the people of Urmun?

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:11.140
The men who had their viscera torn asunder 
for opposing the establishment...

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:14.090
The women who were raped by soldiers...

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:17.090
The children who died of 
starvation and disease...

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:18.970
And Naricia.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:22.080
What way... What words are there to save them?

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:23.090
Tell me!

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:28.600
How do I erase the hell that 
is burned into my retinas?

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:33.480
What you're doing won't save Urmun.

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:38.110
You're just creating more and more Dochettas.

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:44.180
I'll kill as many of those 
enemies as I need to.

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:47.450
All for Naricia and the people of Urmun.

00:19:49.090 --> 00:19:49.750
Don't bother.

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:52.910
He has an Altar-level barrier.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:56.040
You're objectionable.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:20:00.200
You've simply mistaken your 
own will for that of others.

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:02.760
Naricia's will is my will.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:05.140
That's the choice I've made.

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:07.660
You criticize me with impressive words,

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:10.640
but you will not—nor can you—do anything.

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:14.730
Such people mean nothing to me.

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:19.240
You two will not defeat me.

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:28.920
<i>Your communication with 
her is my gift to you.</i>

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:32.540
<i>You did good work, thanks to that.</i>

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:35.820
This scent...

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:37.500
What is it?

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:38.540
Oh, nothing.

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:43.270
<i>Could it be that that lightning was...</i>

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:46.070
Let's go.

00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:47.550
Yeah.

00:20:57.300 --> 00:21:01.840
If only there would be no more 
fighting in Urmun or in the world,

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:04.990
and there could be peace and happiness.

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:06.540
That won't happen.

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:09.660
No matter what, people fight.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:11.080
I know.

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:15.500
But you have to wish 
for it at first, to pray for it,

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:17.180
or nothing will change.

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:24.650
You may be right.

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:27.740
But the first thing I wish for is for you

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:32.680
to be able to keep thinking the way you do.

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:34.020
You're so weird.

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:38.100
That's important to me.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:48.410
Nothing matters more to me than 
to express to you this wish...

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:54.790
No, this prayer. 
Even if I die and turn to dust.

00:21:59.030 --> 00:22:03.590
So together, let's wish, pray, and speak.

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:04.380
Okay.

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:11.130
Even if that wish, that prayer, 
can never come true.

00:22:11.130 --> 00:22:14.360
Even then, with you...

00:23:51.040 --> 00:23:54.030
Our blood and tears will 
surely drench the desert

00:23:54.030 --> 00:23:56.280
at the end of time on this earth.

00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:59.000
We will surely never be complete.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:01.960
We will surely not be standing in paradise.

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:04.460
And yet, and yet, I...

00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:05.040
<b>And Yet, We...</b>
